# omarchy-base.packages — phase-1 additive session stack
# Derived from omacom/omarchy @ quattro (4.0.x), clone commit 3faafba234e530b0986196b98dc2c38951e7dd6f
# Plan: docs/design/omarchy-integration.md + docs/design/omarchy-session-integration.md
#   (phase 1: session-only, no boot-chain contact). Superseded by those design
#   docs; the 2026-09-27 loose plan they grew out of is archived at
#   ~/Projects/etc/hngh-related/jcode-sessions/2026-10-13/notes/
#   2026-09-27-omarchy-integration-plan-SUPERSEDED.md
# Note: omarchy v4 ships no hypridle/hyprlock/hyprpaper — lock screen is owe/owe-lockfeed.
# Marks: `# aur` = genuinely in the AUR (wicket aur-build lane);
# `# omarchy-repo` = ships from upstream's signed [omarchy] pacman repo
# (pkgs.omarchy.org/stable/$arch, upstream default/pacman/pacman-stable.conf)
# — completion there is a repo-add, i.e. a provider-configuration change
# on the certificate lane, NOT a makepkg/AUR build. The dispatcher
# (automation/lib/wicket.sh) defers `# omarchy-repo` lines only while
# the repo is absent from pacman.conf (no uncommented `[omarchy]`
# section — otherwise pacman would refuse the whole transaction on
# target-not-found); once the repo lands there, the lines are included
# in the transaction automatically.

# Hyprland session core
hyprland
uwsm
quickshell
foot
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
hyprland-guiutils
hyprland-preview-share-picker # omarchy-repo
hyprpicker
hyprsunset

# Session utilities (from omarchy-base.packages, session-booting subset)
grim
slurp
cliphist
wl-clipboard
wtype
brightnessctl
pamixer
wireplumber
xdg-terminal-exec

# Lock-screen / desktop-video (v4 uses OWE instead of hyprlock/hypridle)
owe # omarchy-repo
owe-lockfeed # omarchy-repo

